DO-NOT-USE-IN-PROD — sample JWT key placeholder.

This file is intentionally NOT a valid RSA / Ed25519 key. The filename
mirrors the upstream Ardan Labs sample
(https://github.com/ardanlabs/service/blob/master/zarf/keys/54bb2165-71e1-41a6-af3e-7da4a0e1e2c1.pem)
so the layout discipline is identical, but the literal key bytes are not
vendored — every Bodh deployment must generate its own keypair per the
recipe in README.md.

To materialise a real (still-non-prod) key into this slot for local dev:

  openssl genrsa -out 54bb2165-71e1-41a6-af3e-7da4a0e1e2c1.pem 2048

Anything generated locally MUST stay local — `.gitignore` excludes
*.pem files in this directory.
